== Q2  binomial or Poisson
binomial(5, 0.3): mean 1.5  variance 1.0499999999999998  ratio 0.7
Poisson(3): mean 3 variance 3 ratio 1
binomial(10, 0.3) P(2) = 0.2335   Poisson(3) P(2) = 0.2240   variance/mean = 0.7
binomial(100, 0.03) P(2) = 0.2252   Poisson(3) P(2) = 0.2240   variance/mean = 0.97
binomial(1000, 0.003) P(2) = 0.2242   Poisson(3) P(2) = 0.2240   variance/mean = 0.997

== Q3  zero correlation, strong dependence
r(x, y) = -0.010987237330998958  r(x^2, y) = 0.9861756576367757  r(|x|, y) = 0.9541039407945898
E[x^3] for symmetric x is 0; mean of x^3 in the sample: -0.02027037183476259  mean x: 0.021783867877175324
jointly normal and uncorrelated: r = -0.0001858929670734664  r(x^2, y^2) = 0.0025043050945415895

